pth into  the characters that we see in the  original movie and so  our hope is you know if you watch season  three  you'll go again back and watch karate  kid  in a new light even in in a different  way  than if you've seen the first two  seasons because we shed light on certain  things that  you know kind of in some ways set up the  original karate kid movie it's just  because we love these characters and we  want to know more about them and what  makes their heads tick  and you know you get little glimpses for  example of what johnny's life was like  and his home life was like uh on our  show in season one  which gives you something a new  perspective when you watch the original  i think  it's a similar thing in season three we  we have  moments on that show rather moments in  the season  that make you go back to the first movie  and look at it  in a new light and um not just  you know like john said one is with  miyagi but it's with  all the characters and it's it's really  uh  it's fun because you know we're telling  a new fresh story we have a lot of stuff  with  you know the younger actors that have  nothing to do with the past  but you can't escape the past and it's  it's  it's embedded in the story and in the  characters and to understand  the present and the future you kind of  have to go back into the past and  and work things out and and uncover new  things and that's what's fun about  season three  well there's a great lyric in in joe  esposito's uh  timeless song you're the best around  that says history repeats itself  and you know it's in there because that  song was composed for rocky  iii and it was literally supposed to be  history repeats itself as he's you know  fighting again  uh but they use it for the karate kid  where i don't think history had repeated  itself yet  at the time the song was on but by the  time  our audience is seeing season three of  cobra kai there is enough to  to play with now with that younger  generation especially looki